## SEMANTIC EQUIVALENCE REQUIREMENTS

### Auth Semantics (MUST be identical)
| Condition | Current | Target | Status |
|-----------|---------|--------|--------|
| Missing session | 401 | 401 | ✓ Must match |
| Invalid session | 401 | 401 | ✓ Must match |
| Valid session, no workspace | 403 | 403 | ✓ Must match |
| Valid session, workspace denied | 403 | 403 | ✓ Must match |
| Valid session, workspace allowed | 200 | 200 | ✓ Must match |

### Response Semantics (MUST be identical)
| Property | Must Match | Allowed Changes |
|----------|-----------|-----------------|
| Status code | YES | NO |
| Content-Type | YES | NO |
| Response shape | YES | NO |
| Field order | NO | YES (JSON doesn't guarantee order) |
| Field whitespace | NO | YES (JSON can differ in formatting) |
| Null vs undefined | YES | NO |
| Array vs single object | YES | NO |

### Telemetry Semantics (MUST be identical)
| Signal | Must Match |
|--------|-----------|
| Telemetry event type | YES - AUTH_SUCCESS or AUTH_INVALID |
| Telemetry class | YES - same classification |
| Telemetry severity | YES - same severity level |
| Correlation ID | YES - preserved |
| Request ID | YES - preserved |

### Execution Trace (MUST be complete)
All routes must have:
- ✓ AUTH_SUCCESS or AUTH_INVALID event
- ✓ Execution trace with all stages
- ✓ Correlation ID in all logging

---

## MUTATION PROFILE (READ-ONLY, BUT...)

Even read-only routes mutate:
- **Telemetry writes**: Async, non-blocking
- **Audit writes**: Async, non-blocking (if enabled)
- **Cache touches**: May update last-accessed timestamp
- **Metrics increments**: In-memory counters

**CRITICAL**: All mutations MUST be POST-AUTH only.

